        <body>
            <div xml:id="d757">

                <pb facs="0840" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg752"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.81 Buenos Aires/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Buenos Aires</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bailey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-25T17:00:00-04:00">October 25, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13. From Commercial Attaché for Commerce. My 12.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d757-f1"/>
                    Exchange Control Commission rules that prohibition against granting permits
                    applies to all funds destined to pay for merchandise imported prior to February
                    1st, 1933, even if funds deposited in banks to meet documentary drafts. For all
                    other funds prohibition applies as of May 1st. Dye.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bailey</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
